    summary: "AVC-203 (Allo-QuadCAR01-T) is an allogeneic CRISPR-engineered dual-targeting switchable CAR-T cell therapy from AvenCell Therapeutics, with AvenCell Europe GmbH as partner. Off-the-shelf donor CAR-T cells, CRISPR-engineered, that target cells expressing CD19 and/or CD20, built on the switchable RevCAR receptor so other targets can be added through bridging proteins. Its furthest stage is phase 1, for relapsed/refractory B-cell malignancies and diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. No clinical trial naming it is registered on ClinicalTrials.gov. First patient dosed in phase 1 QUADvance in April 2026 (company release 2 April 2026); registry phase 1/2 recruiting (NCT07284433). It has not been shown to work in people.",
